    Make SI:FIND-FOREIGN-SYMBOL work in a static iOS image
    
    Two independent problems, both of which have to be fixed before CFFI can run
    on iOS -- its ECL backend resolves foreign functions by name.
    
    configure ties ENABLE_DLOPEN to --enable-shared, but they are not the same
    question. An iOS app must link statically, and can still dlsym its own
    symbols. build.sh now defines it for the cross builds.
    
    That alone got as far as "Could not load foreign symbol from module :DEFAULT",
    because ecl_library_symbol calls dlsym(0, symbol) for :DEFAULT. A null handle
    is not the global scope on Darwin -- RTLD_DEFAULT is (void *)-2 -- so it always
    returned NULL. In a static image RTLD_DEFAULT is the only way to reach symbols
    that are all in the main executable anyway.
    
    Verified in the simulator: objc_getClass resolves at #x1800579D8 and returns
    the NSString class at #x1F3911FB0.
    
